 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Pretty much, with a bit left over. Most long rides don't go much further than that. Roughly three and a half hours, including stops. It is. Plan to start early and take a lunch break, and you should finish before the afternoon rush. Nice way to build up the distance. Do a twenty mile ride weekend before, and you'll be well prepared. Three to four weeks is enough for a 100 mile ride. Build up the mileage, and mix in easy rides that feel easy on last long day.",
